A '''brown mushroom''' is a [[fungus]] found in the [[Overworld]] and [[the Nether]]. It can only be {{control|placed|text=planted}} in [[mycelium]], [[nylium]], [[podzol]], or darkness,{{until|je 26.4|be 26.60}} which also allows it to spread over time or receive [[bone meal]] to grow into a [[Huge Mushroom|huge brown mushroom]].

== Obtaining ==
=== Breaking ===
Brown mushrooms can be [[instant mining|instantly mined]] with any tool, including by hand.

A brown mushroom also breaks instantly and drops as an item if:
* the block below it is moved or destroyed
* a [[fluid]] flows over it
* a block next to it changes state, but only when it is ''not'' on [[podzol]], [[mycelium]], or [[nylium]] and light level is 13 or higher
{{breaking row|Brown Mushroom|horizontal=1}}

=== Natural generation ===
Brown mushrooms naturally generate in poorly lit areas ([[light level]] of 12 or less). If this condition is met, each [[chunk]] has a {{frac|1|4}} (25.0%) chance to generate brown mushrooms in the form of [[random patch]]es.<ref>{{IN|java}}, they rarely generate because they cannot generate underground due to {{bug|MC-244162}}.</ref>

Brown mushrooms also generate on the surface of a [[swamp|swamp under the trees]], [[old growth spruce taiga]], [[old growth pine taiga]], or [[mushroom fields]] biome, along with anywhere in [[the Nether]]. Unlike plants, they are able to generate on top of nearly any block type.

{{IN|java}}, brown mushrooms are commonly found in patches on the [[Nether roof]], and alongside red mushrooms are the only blocks that can generate there. 

Brown mushrooms also generate inside "mushroom farm" rooms in [[woodland mansion]]s.

[[Fallen tree]]s can have up to 2 mushrooms generated on them.

Brown mushrooms also generate as part of [[abandoned camp]]s in [[dappled forest]]s.

{{block distribution|Brown Mushroom}}

=== Huge mushrooms ===
Breaking a [[brown mushroom block]] drops 0-2 brown mushrooms. [[Fortune]] does not affect the drop rate of mushrooms in any form.<ref>{{bug|MC-156657||Fortune doesn't work on mushroom blocks|Invalid}}</ref>

=== Mob loot ===
[[Shear]]ing a brown [[mooshroom]] drops 5 brown mushrooms and permanently turns it into a normal [[cow]].

Shearing a [[bogged]] drops 2 mushrooms, both of which can be brown.

An [[enderman]] holding a brown mushroom drops it upon death.

{{IN|bedrock}}, [[wandering traders]] have a chance of 25% (increased by 1% per level of [[Looting]]) to drop 3 brown mushrooms when killed while showing the item as trade offer, if the player holds an [[emerald]].

=== Generated loot ===
{{LootChestItem|brown-mushroom}}

=== Trading ===
[[Wandering trader]]s may sell 3 brown mushrooms for 1 [[emerald]].
{{Trade sources}}

== Usage ==
=== Planting ===
Mushrooms can be planted and grown on blocks that have a full top surface in [[light]] levels below 13{{until|je 26.4|be 26.60}} and not directly underneath the sky. They cannot be planted on the top surfaces of [[Slab|slabs]] or [[stairs]].<ref>{{bug|MC-146825}}</ref> For more information, see [[Opacity/Placement]]. If planted on [[mycelium]], [[podzol]] or [[nylium]], they can stay planted in any light level, including skylight. Both brown and red mushrooms grow at the same rate regardless of the light level.<ref name="Fully-Automated Tests of Mushroom Growth at Different Light Levels Using BUD Switch Harvester">http://www.youtube.com/watch?feature=player_detailpage&v=ALkf-b7MbBI&t=864s</ref><ref name="Large scale automated test with additional info">{{ytl|J7AmGnpMCng}}</ref>

=== Huge mushrooms ===
{{main|Huge Mushroom#Growth}}
When [[bone meal]] is applied to a brown mushroom, the mushroom has a chance to grow into a brown [[huge mushroom]], provided that it is on a proper block ([[grass block]], [[dirt]], [[coarse dirt]], [[rooted dirt]], [[mud]], [[muddy mangrove roots]], [[moss block]], or [[pale moss block]] at a light level of 12 or below; on [[podzol]], [[mycelium]] or [[nylium]] at any light level) and is free of [[solid block]]s within 5 blocks ''directly'' above the mushroom.

=== Spread ===
{{See also|Tutorial:Mushroom farming}}

When receiving a [[random tick]], a brown mushroom has a 4% chance of spreading to a nearby block (including even above and below diagonally) if there are fewer than five brown mushrooms in a 9×9×3 volume around the original brown mushroom. Mushrooms can only spread in light levels of 13 or lower.

=== Light source ===
Brown mushrooms emit a barely visible [[light level]] of 1.<ref>{{bug|MC-832|||WAI}}</ref> However, they do not emit light in flower pots.<ref>{{bug|MC-200055}}</ref>

=== Decoration ===
Brown mushrooms can be planted in a [[flower pot]].

=== Crafting ingredient ===
{{crafting usage|Brown Mushroom}}

=== Composting ===
Placing a brown mushroom into a [[composter]] has a 65% chance of raising the compost level by 1.

== Sounds ==
Despite being a fungus, brown mushrooms use the grass sound set, unlike other blocks such as Nether fungi and shelf mushrooms. Mojang have stated that this is not a valid discrepancy to address.<ref>{{bug|MC-170906}}</ref>

